  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NESA Center Indo-Pacific Oceans Workshop 01-26</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In mid-March 2026, the NESA Center shall virtually host the Indo-Pacific Oceans Workshop. This program, targeted towards operators who work on maritime security, shall hear from leading subject matter experts, policymakers, and practitioners on how states can more effectively use new tools to enhance maritime capability. Specific issues to be addressed include public-private partnerships for integrating emerging technology, advances in underwater domain awareness, supply chain enhancements and protection, maritime ISR, and cross-domain tools to protect regional waters. The workshop has a regional focus on the Indo-Pacific, but the lessons focused upon cover all regions of the world. Thus, what may afflict the maritime security services of a Southeast Asian country may also be the same variables that burden a country in Central America, East Africa, or the Pacific. Through the three days, participants will have the opportunity to share their own experiences in the maritime domain along with being provided access to a set of new digital tools developed by NESA to assist in a long-term community of interest tied to maritime security.</narrative>
  </description>
